(QUARTERLY CLOSE AUDIT REPORT) Tj T*
(Dungeon Crawl: Seattle, Floor 5, the Estuary) Tj T*
(Prepared by: the Quarterly Close Accountant, Office of the Controller) Tj T*
(Scope: round one of the dance-off at the Pier 59 collapse, and the party's Groove ledger) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Finding 1: Groove booked as revenue.) Tj T*
(The party recorded the Groove it kept after round one as income. Groove is a derived) Tj T*
(stat, not money. It cannot be banked, sold or carried into the next quarter, and it) Tj T*
(comes back in full when a Crawler rests in a Safe Room \(Crawl Handbook, Groove, Mana,) Tj T*
(Benched and Cancelled\). Recommended remediation: stop asking the auditor to invoice it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Finding 2: Unreported Ink Cloud.) Tj T*
(During round one, the party leader, Barnaby, released an Ink Cloud that left the) Tj T*
(pickleweed slick for two rounds. No receipt was filed. The auditor danced Off-Beat for) Tj T*
(both rounds and wishes this noted in the record.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Finding 3: Tide schedule not disclosed.) Tj T*
(The Estuary dance floor floods twice a day. Neither party disclosed the tide table) Tj T*
(before the dance-off began. The auditor recommends that every future dance-off on this) Tj T*
(floor start with a look at the tide.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
